/*  How deep a value a call or a member read hands back lives — `ComputeReturnDepthSignature`,
    `PopulateCastDepthCache`, `ComputeMemberAccessDepth` and `ValueDepthOf` in
    `src/Interpreter/TypeChecker.Functions.cs`, `.Objects.cs` and `.Rabbit.cs`.

    ★ Once a function's body has been checked, where what it gives back can LIVE is worked out —
    its RETURN-DEPTH SIGNATURE: the 0-based positions of the parameters it may come from, -1 for
    the object a method or getter is called on, and -2 for something the function MADE, or anything
    that cannot be traced to a parameter. At a call, the value handed back is as deep as the
    deepest argument in those positions — and, when the signature holds -2, as deep as the call
    itself: a call opens no region, so what a function makes lies in whatever region its caller
    has open (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O1).

    ★ The walk reaches every `Return`, `Define` and `becomes` in the body, whatever holds them, and
    stops only at a body that returns for itself. A name carries everything it was ever given.

    ★ A name whose function has no signature yet — a recursive call, a lambda, one declared later —
    is not traced: it may be any reference-typed parameter, or something made.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    // ── The signature ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Where what this body gives back can live — ascending, -1 for `one`, -2 for something made.
    Bind series of number to return-depth-signature unto checker, given (the node parameters, the node body, the fact with-receiver):
        Define positions as a map from text to number.
        Define referenced as a series of number.
        Define index as 0.
        For each parameter in parameters's children, repeat:
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            In positions, the entry for name becomes index.
            If cast is-reference-type on (cast one's resolved on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1))), insert index into referenced.
            Increment index by 1.
        Done.
        If with-receiver:
            In positions, the entry for "one" becomes -1.
            Insert -1 into referenced.
        Done.
        Define gathered as a series of node.
        Cast gather-depth-nodes on (body, gathered).

        // Every name the body gives a value to starts empty, so that a name read before the walk
        // has reached its `Define` is not taken for one the walk knows nothing about.
        Define locals as a map from text to series of number.
        For each statement in gathered, repeat:
            If cast gives-a-name on (statement's kind):
                Define target-name as cast depth-target-name on (statement).
                If the entry for target-name in locals is void, in locals, the entry for target-name becomes a series of number.
            Done.
        Done.

        // To a fixed point: a loop can carry a value from its end back to its start, and the
        // sets only ever grow, so this ends.
        Define grew as true.
        While grew, repeat:
            The grew becomes false.
            For each statement in gathered, repeat:
                If cast gives-a-name on (statement's kind):
                    Define carried as the entry for cast depth-target-name on (statement) in locals.
                    If carried is not void:
                        Define reaching as cast one's symbolic-depth on (cast depth-target-value on (statement), positions, referenced, locals).
                        For each one-index in reaching, repeat:
                            If cast holds-number on (carried, one-index) is false:
                                Insert one-index into carried.
                                The grew becomes true.
                            Done.
                        Done.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.

        Define flows as a series of number.
        For each statement in gathered, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ReturnStatement":
                If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) is false:
                    Cast union-into on (cast one's symbolic-depth on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), positions, referenced, locals), flows).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define ascending as a series of number.
        Define candidate as -2.
        While candidate is less than the number of parameters's children, repeat:
            If cast holds-number on (flows, candidate), insert candidate into ascending.
            Increment candidate by 1.
        Done.
        Return ascending.
    Done.

    /// Adds each index not already held.
    Bind void to union-into, given (the series of number source, the series of number held):
        For each one-index in source, repeat:
            If cast holds-number on (held, one-index) is false, insert one-index into held.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A body that returns for itself: what it gives back is its own, and so are its names.
    Bind fact to owns-its-returns, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "BindStatement" or kind is "LambdaLiteral" or kind is "LaunchTaskStatement" or kind is "ObjectDefinition"
            or kind is "GetterDeclaration" or kind is "SetterDeclaration" or kind is "UnmakerDeclaration"
            or kind is "OperatorOverloadDeclaration".
    Done.

    /// A statement that gives a name a value. An iterator is an element of what it walks, and `it`
    /// in a `Judge` is the subject: both live no deeper than what they came from.
    Bind fact to gives-a-name, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "DefineStatement" or kind is "BecomesStatement" or kind is "ForEachStatement" or kind is "JudgeStatement".
    Done.

    Bind text to depth-target-name, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        If kind is "JudgeStatement", return "it".
        If kind is "ForEachStatement":
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)), return "it".
        Done.
        Return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
    Done.

    Bind node to depth-target-value, given (the node statement):
        If statement's kind is "JudgeStatement", return cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Return cast field-of on (statement, 2).
    Done.

    /// Every statement of a body that gives a name a value or returns one, however deep.
    Bind void to gather-depth-nodes, given (the node branch, the series of node gathered):
        Define kind as branch's kind.
        If cast owns-its-returns on (kind), return.
        If kind is "ReturnStatement" or cast gives-a-name on (kind), insert branch into gathered.
        For each part in branch's children, repeat:
            Cast gather-depth-nodes on (part, gathered).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Every reference-typed parameter.
    Bind series of number to all-referenced, given (the series of number referenced):
        Define copied as a series of number.
        For each one-index in referenced, repeat:
            Insert one-index into copied.
        Done.
        Return copied.
    Done.

    /// What cannot be traced: any reference-typed parameter, or something made.
    Bind series of number to untraced, given (the series of number referenced):
        Define copied as cast all-referenced on (referenced).
        Insert -2 into copied.
        Return copied.
    Done.

    /// Where this expression's value may come from. Empty: it lives outside every region.
    Bind series of number to symbolic-depth unto checker, given (the node said, the map from text to number positions,
            the series of number referenced, the map from text to series of number locals):
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "VariableReference":
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1)).
            Define spot as the entry for name in positions.
            If spot is not void:
                If cast holds-number on (referenced, spot), return a series with (spot).
                Return a series of number.
            Done.
            Define local as the entry for name in locals.
            If local is not void:
                Define copied as a series of number.
                For each one-index in local, repeat:
                    Insert one-index into copied.
                Done.
                Return copied.
            Done.
            // A top-level constant is made before any region opens. Any other name — one captured
            // from an enclosing function, or bound by a statement this walk does not model — is
            // not traced.
            Define seen as cast one's look-up on (name).
            If seen is not void:
                If seen's permanent and seen's parameter is false, return a series of number.
            Done.
            Return cast untraced on (referenced).
        Done.
        If kind is "CastExpression":
            Define callee as cast field-of on (said, 1).
            If callee's kind is "VariableReference":
                Define callee-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)).
                Define found as cast one's look-up on (callee-name).
                If found is not void:
                    If found's shape's kind is "FunctionType":
                        Define signature as the entry for "{callee-name}@{found's line}" in one's depth-signatures.
                        If signature is void, return cast untraced on (referenced).
                        Define reached as a series of number.
                        Define given-args as (cast field-of on (said, 2))'s children.
                        For each one-index in signature, repeat:
                            If one-index is -2:
                                If cast holds-number on (reached, -2) is false, insert -2 into reached.
                            Done.
                            Otherwise if one-index is -1:
                                // Which argument was the receiver is settled by dispatch, not here.
                                For each argument in given-args, repeat:
                                    Cast union-into on (cast one's symbolic-depth on (argument, positions, referenced, locals), reached).
                                Done.
                            Done.
                            Otherwise if one-index is less than the number of given-args:
                                Cast union-into on (cast one's symbolic-depth on (item (one-index + 1) of given-args, positions, referenced, locals), reached).
                            Done.
                        Done.
                        Return reached.
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
            Return cast untraced on (referenced).
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesAccess" or kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Return cast one's symbolic-depth on (cast field-of on (said, 1), positions, referenced, locals).
        Done.
        If kind is "MapLookup":
            Return cast one's symbolic-depth on (cast field-of on (said, 1), positions, referenced, locals).
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral" or kind is "MapLiteral" or kind is "MatrixLiteral" or kind is "MatrixSized"
                or kind is "RangeExpression" or kind is "ChannelCreation":
            // Made here, which is wherever the caller is.
            Return a series with (-2).
        Done.
        // A missed flow has to cost a refusal: "nothing reaches it" is the unsound answer.
        Return cast untraced on (referenced).
    Done.

    // ── At a call, and at a member read ───────────────────────────────────

    Bind text to node-place, given (the node said, the number line-field):
        Return "{(cast field-of on (said, line-field))'s word}:{(cast field-of on (said, line-field + 1))'s word}".
    Done.

    /// `ValueDepthOf`: how deep the value an expression gives lives.
    Bind number to depth-of-value unto checker, given (the node said, the node shape):
        If cast is-reference-type on (shape) is false, return 0.
        Define kind as said's kind.
        If kind is "VariableReference":
            Define found as cast one's look-up on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (said, 1))).
            If found is not void, return found's depth.
            Return 0.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral" or kind is "MapLiteral" or kind is "MatrixLiteral" or kind is "MatrixSized"
                or kind is "ObjectLiteral" or kind is "RangeExpression" or kind is "ChannelCreation":
            Return one's rabbit-depth.
        Done.
        If kind is "CastExpression":
            Define cached as the entry for cast node-place on (said, 3) in one's call-depths.
            If cached is not void, return cached.
        Done.
        If kind is "PossessiveAccess" or kind is "RecordNamedAccess":
            Define cached-member as the entry for cast node-place on (said, 3) in one's member-depths.
            If cached-member is not void, return cached-member.
        Done.
        Return 0.
    Done.

    /// The type a method is written in — its own, or one it embeds.
    Bind text to method-owner unto checker, given (the text owner, the text method-name):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (owner).
        If definition is void, return owner.
        For each method in cast one's all-methods on (definition), repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (method, 1)) is method-name, return owner.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "", return owner.
        Return cast one's method-owner on (embedded, method-name).
    Done.

    /// `PopulateCastDepthCache`: what a call gives back is as deep as its deepest argument in the
    /// positions its callee's signature names, and as deep as the call itself when the callee may
    /// have made it.
    Bind void to record-call-depth unto checker, given (the node said, the call reached, the node call-args, the node gives):
        If cast is-reference-type on (gives) is false, return.
        Define callee as cast field-of on (said, 1).
        Define receiver as cast unknown-type.
        Define given-args as call-args's children.
        Define validated as a series of node.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in given-args, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If place is greater than reached's receivers, insert argument into validated.
        Done.
        If reached's receivers is greater than 0 and the number of given-args is greater than 0:
            The receiver becomes item 1 of given-args.
        Done.
        Otherwise if callee's kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            The receiver becomes cast field-of on (callee, 1).
        Done.
        Define deepest as 0.
        Define signature as the entry for reached's depth-key in one's depth-signatures.
        // Nothing known about the callee: what it gives back may be something it made.
        If signature is void, the deepest becomes one's rabbit-depth.
        If signature is not void:
            For each one-index in signature, repeat:
                If one-index is -2 and one's rabbit-depth is greater than deepest, the deepest becomes one's rabbit-depth.
                Define reaching as cast unknown-type.
                If one-index is -1, the reaching becomes receiver.
                Otherwise if one-index is not less than 0 and one-index is less than the number of validated:
                    The reaching becomes item (one-index + 1) of validated.
                Done.
                If cast is-none on (reaching) is false:
                    Define reaching-type as cast one's infer on (reaching) but on failure cast unknown-type.
                    Define reaching-depth as cast one's depth-of-value on (reaching, reaching-type).
                    If reaching-depth is greater than deepest, the deepest becomes reaching-depth.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        In one's call-depths, the entry for cast node-place on (said, 3) becomes deepest.
    Done.

    /// The signature key of a method reached through an object of this type.
    Bind text to method-depth-key unto checker, given (the node target-type, the text member):
        If target-type's kind is not "ObjectType", return "".
        Return "{cast one's method-owner on (cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target-type, 1)), member)}'s {member}".
    Done.

    /// `ComputeMemberAccessDepth`: a field lives inside its object; a getter's value does too,
    /// unless its signature says it makes something new.
    Bind void to record-member-depth unto checker, given (the node said, the node target, the text owner, the text member):
        Define target-type as cast one's infer on (target) but on failure cast unknown-type.
        Define receiver-depth as cast one's depth-of-value on (target, target-type).
        Define depth as receiver-depth.
        Define getter-owner as cast one's getter-owner on (owner, member).
        If getter-owner is not "":
            Define signature as the entry for "{getter-owner}\t{member}" in one's getter-signatures.
            If signature is not void:
                If cast holds-number on (signature, -1) is false, the depth becomes 0.
                If cast holds-number on (signature, -2) and one's rabbit-depth is greater than depth, the depth becomes one's rabbit-depth.
            Done.
        Done.
        In one's member-depths, the entry for cast node-place on (said, 3) becomes depth.
    Done.

    /// The type a getter is written in — its own, or one it embeds — or "".
    Bind text to getter-owner unto checker, given (the text owner, the text getter-name):
        Define definition as cast one's definition-of on (owner).
        If definition is void, return "".
        For each getter in cast one's all-getters on (definition), repeat:
            If cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (getter, 1)) is getter-name, return owner.
        Done.
        Define embedded as cast embedded-name on (definition).
        If embedded is "", return "".
        Return cast one's getter-owner on (embedded, getter-name).
    Done.
Done.
